{"family": "metric3d", "task": "depth", "name": "Metric3D v2", "plain": "Metric3D v2 (Wei Yin and Mu Hu et al.): metric depth and surface normals from one image, given the focal length. Commercially usable; the authors ask commercial users to contact them.", "summary": "Metric3D v2 (Hu et al. 2024): metric depth and surface normals from one image; a DINOv2-reg ViT-L encoder and a RAFT-style iterative depth / normal decoder in a canonical camera space (focal 1000 px), rescaled by the given focal length.", "tier": "stable", "upstream": "https://github.com/YvanYin/Metric3D", "upstream_commit": "eb5b6fa", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "Metric3Dv2: A Versatile Monocular Geometric Foundation Model for Zero-shot Metric Depth and Surface Normal Estimation", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.15506", "date": "2024-03-22", "venue": "TPAMI 2024", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["fastbb", "dpt_fused"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "options": [], "outputs": [{"name": "depth", "extra": false}, {"name": "normals", "extra": false}, {"name": "confidence", "extra": false}], "output_info": {"kind": "metric"}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": ["The upstream README says 'for further commercial inquiries, please contact' the authors; no weights licence is stated, so the BSD-2-Clause code licence is assumed."], "limitations": [], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: a depth or inverse-depth map. `kind` (a card field, `result.kind`) says what the numbers mean: `metric` = metres; `scale_invariant`, `affine_invariant` and `affine_invariant_inverse` are relative (unknown scale or shift, not metres). Metric models that use the focal length take `model(image, intrinsics=K)` (K `[3, 3]`, pixels of the input): `metric3d-vit-large` and `da3metric-large` need it for correct metres (`da3metric-large`: metres = output x focal / 300; without `intrinsics=` a 300 px focal length is assumed, wrong for a real camera). `unidepth-v2-vitl14`, `unik3d-vitl`, `depth-pro` and MoGe estimate the camera themselves (given `intrinsics=` replace `fx`); `zoedepth-nk` and the relative models (`da3mono-large` too) take none. Normals-only models (`kind` `none`) return `result.normals` `[B, H, W, 3]` (unit vectors, camera frame: x right, y down, z forward).", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "metric3d-vit-large", "released": "0.1.1", "added_in": "0.1.0", "ref": "metric3d-vit-large@1", "name": "metric3d-vit-large", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {}, "licence": {"code": "BSD-2-Clause", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "BSD-2-Clause (assumed from code)", "weights_assumed": true, "evidence": "https://github.com/YvanYin/Metric3D/blob/eb5b6fac0dc155e4e52f576e304fbf11655ff339/README.md#license-and-contact", "training_data": [{"id": "unstated", "name": "not stated by the authors"}], "training_note": "16M images from 18 public metric-depth datasets (indoor, outdoor, driving) per the Metric3D v2 paper (arXiv 2404.15506); original asks commercial users to contact the authors", "commercial": "yes", "reasons": [], "notes": ["weights licence not stated by the original authors; assumed to be the code licence", "data: unstated"]}, "weights": [{"name": "metric_depth_vit_large_800k.pth", "sha256": "15328ffc42b528b95f188687418f6f03b3f123eb34ccdbd686c112abbea6d972", "size": 1647972663, "url": "https://huggingface.co/JUGGHM/Metric3D/resolve/80d2d1410afb4b23cd9d18c6be9144483d4b70b6/metric_depth_vit_large_800k.pth", "host": "Hugging Face", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mirror": null}], "input_size": "any H x W >= 8, resized or padded inside the model", "tested_max": {"size": "3000x4000", "alloc_mib": 2401, "reserved_mib": 2926}, "speed": {"standard": "994x1482", "inputs": [{"input": "518x770", "scene": "synthetic", "standard": false, "modes": {"origi